cB,kjX=[0,by,[0,g,a9w]],kjY=dv,kjZ=[0,bq,[0,g,dv]],kj0=[0,[0,ik,[0,U,[0,[0,bq,[0,g,hf]],[0,[0,hM,[0,U,[0,[0,f4,[0,U,[0,pnc,pnb]]],[0,[0,iB,[0,U,pnd]],0]]]],[0,[0,fY,[0,h,[0,[0,g,f4],[0,[0,g,iB],0]]]],0]]]]],0],kj1=cB,kj2=[0,by,[0,g,a7J]],kj3=dv,kj4=[0,bq,[0,g,dv]],kj5="\nPlaces the **statics** refractor on the bindings at the given paths: a GUI type-ascription overlay (offside type cell) for human-readable types on expressions.\nThis does not change program text. If a runtime probe is on the same binding, it is replaced by statics (same transition as the editor\xe2\x80\x99s statics toggle).\nCollapsed definitions are auto-expanded when statics are placed so overlays are visible.\n\nParameters:\npaths: list(string) \xe2\x80\x94 paths to the bindings\n\nSee the system prompt **Projectors and the agent view** for how statics relate to probes and livelits.\n",kj6=[0,[0,ik,[0,U,[0,[0,bq,[0,g,hf]],[0,[0,hM,[0,U,[0,[0,iB,[0,U,[0,pnf,pne]]],0]]],[0,[0,fY,[0,h,[0,[0,g,iB],0]]],0]]]]],0],kj7=cB,kj8=[0,by,[0,g,a9f]],kj9=dv,kj_=[0,bq,[0,g,dv]],kj$="\nRemoves **only** the statics refractor from the bindings at the given paths.\nRuntime probes on the same binding are left unchanged (unlike remove_probe).\n\nParameters:\npaths: list(string) \xe2\x80\x94 paths to the bindings to clear statics overlays from\n",kka=[0,[0,ik,[0,U,[0,[0,bq,[0,g,hf]],[0,[0,hM,[0,U,[0,[0,iB,[0,U,[0,pnh,png]]],0]]],[0,[0,fY,[0,h,[0,[0,g,iB],0]]],0]]]]],0],kkb=cB,kkc=[0,by,[0,g,bdy]],kkd=dv,kke=[0,bq,[0,g,dv]],kkf="\nToggles the statics refractor on or off for the bindings at the given paths (same behavior as the editor statics toggle).\nCollapsed definitions are auto-expanded when statics end up enabled.\n\nParameters:\npaths: list(string) \xe2\x80\x94 paths to the bindings to toggle\n",kkg=[0,[0,ik,[0,U,[0,[0,bq,[0,g,hf]],[0,[0,hM,[0,U,[0,[0,iB,[0,U,[0,pnj,pni]]],0]]],[0,[0,fY,[0,h,[0,[0,g,iB],0]]],0]]]]],0],kkh=cB,kki=[0,by,[0,g,a$H]],kkj=dv,kkk=[0,bq,[0,g,dv]],kkl=[0,l],kkm=[0,he],kko=[0,"- **checkbox** \xe2\x80\x94 Toggle UI for boolean literals."],kkp=[0,"- **slider** \xe2\x80\x94 Numeric literal editor (integer)."],kkq=[0,"- **sliderf** \xe2\x80\x94 Numeric literal editor (floating-point)."],kkr=[0,"- **card** \xe2\x80\x94 **Playing-card** editor: a tuple `(Suit, Rank)` such as `(Hearts, Ace)` or a list of those tuples. **Not** for records, modules, or `{ let \xe2\x80\xa6; \xe2\x80\xa6 }` blocks."],kks=[0,"- **livelit** \xe2\x80\x94 Custom livelit projector for structured literal editing."],kkt=[0,"- **text** \xe2\x80\x94 Multiline string literal editor."],kku=[0,"- **table** \xe2\x80\x94 Spreadsheet-style editor for a **list of labeled tuples** sharing the same labels; the labels become column headers. Attaches off the **elaborated** form, so it can apply where the surface syntax alone is not yet a table."],kkv=[0,"- **csv** \xe2\x80\x94 CSV **file import** UI. Attaches only when the definition is the **empty list** `[]`; after placement, import fills it with row/tuple syntax. Non-empty lists (e.g. `[1, 2, 3]`) **cannot** take this projector."],kkw=[0,0,0],kkx=[0,l,[0,"These are alternative UIs for literals and structured values that may already appear in code.",0]],kky=[0,"### Livelits (menu projectors)",0],kkA=[0,l,0],kkB=[0,l,[0,"### Syntax projector tools (Filbert)",[0,"`place_syntax_projector(kind, paths)`, `remove_syntax_projector(paths)`, and `toggle_syntax_projector(kind, paths)` apply **syntax projector** UIs to the term selected by each path.",[0,"`kind` must be a menu projector name (`fold`, `slider`, `sliderf`, `check`, `text`, `card`, `csv`, `table`, `livelit`) \xe2\x80\x94 not `probe` or `statics` (those use the probe/statics tools).",[0,l,[0,"**CRITICAL \xe2\x80\x94 livelits are not automatic:** Ordinary Hazel code (`let speed = 50`, `let is_active = true`, list literals, records) renders as **plain text** until you call **`place_syntax_projector`**.",[0,'If the user asks how livelits work, or wants sliders/checkboxes/CSV editors/text boxes, you **must** call `place_syntax_projector` with the right `kind` on each binding path (e.g. `slider` on `"speed"`, `check` on `"is_active"`, `text` on `"message"`, `csv` only when the RHS is `[]`, `card` only on playing-card tuples/lists\xe2\x80\x94see livelit lines above; nested paths like `"config/volume"`).',[0,"**Never** describe interactive widgets as present based only on `insert_*`, `update_*`, or other edit tools \xe2\x80\x94 that is false unless the matching `place_syntax_projector` calls succeeded.",[0,l,0]]]]]]]]],kkC=io(["## Projectors and the agent view",l,"### Fold (`\xe2\x8b\xb1`)","A **fold** is a collapsed definition in the GUI: the definition shows as `\xe2\x8b\xb1` (not source text).","Use `expand` / `collapse` (see **Paths** and **View Tools** above).",l,"### Runtime probe refractor","The **probe** refractor attaches to a binding and shows evaluated values in the agent view (e.g. `expr \xe2\x89\xa1 value`).","Tools: `place_probe`, `remove_probe`, `toggle_probe`.",l,"### Statics refractor (type overlay)","The **statics** refractor shows a type ascription overlay in the GUI (offside type cell) for human clarity.","It does not change program text; the agent\xe2\x80\x99s printed context may not mirror the overlay unless printing is extended.",l]),kkE=[0,"**Projectors**: **Folds** display as `\xe2\x8b\xb1` (collapsed defs; expand/collapse in the full prompt).",[0,"**Refractors** overlay bindings: **probes** show runtime values (`\xe2\x89\xa1` in context); **statics** add a type overlay in the GUI.",[0,"**Livelits** are alternate UIs for literals (checkbox, slider/sliderf, text, card, csv, table, livelit, plus fold in the menu).",[0,"**Agent tools**: `place_syntax_projector` / `remove_syntax_projector` / `toggle_syntax_projector` (see full prompt).",[0,"Full detail lives in Filbert\xe2\x80\x99s live system prompt **Projectors and the agent view** section (this excerpt may be truncated).",0]]]]],kkJ="Editor.Meta.t_of_yojson",kkI="Editor.Meta.yojson_of_t",